# Shell scripts must keep LF line endings regardless of the checking-out
# OS's line-ending config - a CRLF shebang ("#!/bin/sh\r") is not a valid
# shebang and fails to execute at all. Found while adding githooks/pre-push:
# this repo had no .gitattributes at all, so Windows' core.autocrlf=true
# (a common Git-for-Windows default) would silently corrupt these on
# checkout for any Windows contributor.
*.sh text eol=lf
githooks/* text eol=lf
